1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:02,670
OKAY, GUYS, LISTEN.

2
00:00:02,711 --> 00:00:03,796
DON'T FORGET THAT TOMORROW

3
00:00:03,838 --> 00:00:05,380
IS THE DAY
EMILY GETS MARRIED AGAIN

4
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:06,757
SO, WHATEVER WE DO

5
00:00:06,799 --> 00:00:08,467
JUST TRY TO REALLY
KEEP ROSS'S MIND OFF OF IT.

6
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:09,593
OH, YEAH, GOOD IDEA.

7
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:12,262
HEY, MAN, WHAT'S UP?

8
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:15,850
OH, JUST THINKING ABOUT EMILY
GETTING MARRIED TOMORROW.

9
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:20,312
OH, ROSS, LOOK! LOOK!

10
00:00:21,689 --> 00:00:22,731
WHAT? WHERE?

11
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:24,399
RIGHT OVER THERE.
RIGHT THERE.

12
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:26,652
LOOK, LOOK, LOOK.

13
00:00:26,694 --> 00:00:28,278
WHAT AM I LOOKING AT?

14
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:31,156
SOMEBODY HELP ME OUT HERE.

15
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:32,157
HEY.
HELLO.

16
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:33,450
HI.
HOW ARE YOU?

17
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:35,953
MONICA, SORRY I DIDN'T
COME BY LAST NIGHT.

18
00:00:35,995 --> 00:00:37,412
I WAS OUT WITH GARY.

19
00:00:37,454 --> 00:00:40,081
HE LET ME RIDE
AROUND WITH HIM
IN HIS COP CAR.

20
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,876
WE SAW AND
PREVENTED CRIMES.

21
00:00:41,917 --> 00:00:43,293
YOU GOT TO GO
ON A RIDE-ALONG?

22
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:44,336
UH-HUH.

23
00:00:44,378 --> 00:00:45,671
I WANT TO GO ON A RIDE-ALONG.

24
00:00:45,713 --> 00:00:46,839
ME, TOO.

25
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:47,840
OKAY.

26
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:48,716
YEAH, ME, TOO.

27
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,718
REALLY? YOU?

28
00:00:52,845 --> 00:00:54,596
YEAH.

29
00:00:54,638 --> 00:00:56,264
I MEAN,
IT'S KIND OF DANGEROUS.

30
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:58,684
WELL, I LIKE DANGER.

31
00:00:58,726 --> 00:01:00,059
OKAY, YOU GUYS FREE TONIGHT?

32
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:02,021
YEAH.
YEAH.

33
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:03,522
TONIGHT? Y-YOU DIDN'T SAY

34
00:01:03,564 --> 00:01:05,524
IT WAS GOING
TO BE AT NIGHTTIME.

35
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:17,369
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

36
00:01:17,411 --> 00:01:19,663
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

37
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:22,332
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

38
00:01:22,374 --> 00:01:27,212
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

39
00:01:27,254 --> 00:01:29,924
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

40
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:32,091
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

41
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:35,971
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

42
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:38,181
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

43
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,851
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

44
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:42,269
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

45
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:45,981
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

46
00:01:46,023 --> 00:01:49,902
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

47
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,621
HEY.
HEY.

48
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:02,039
I THOUGHT TONIGHT

49
00:02:02,081 --> 00:02:03,624
WE COULD FINALLY ORGANIZE
THESE PHOTOS.

50
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,876
OH, THANK GOD!

51
00:02:05,918 --> 00:02:07,335
FINALLY!

52
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,670
OKAY.

53
00:02:08,712 --> 00:02:10,589
I'VE BROKEN THEM DOWN
INTO CATEGORIES, OKAY?

54
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:12,925
WE HAVE, UH,
WE GOT HOLIDAYS,
BIRTHDAYS, CANDIDS.

55
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:14,426
AND THEN WHAT I'VE DONE IS

56
00:02:14,468 --> 00:02:16,762
I'VE CROSS-REFERENCED THEM
BY SUBJECT, RIGHT?

57
00:02:16,804 --> 00:02:18,013
SO IF YOU'RE
LOOKING UP

58
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:21,141
LET'S SAY,
"BIRTHDAYS" AND "DOGS"

59
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,435
YOU GET PHOTO 152. SEE?

60
00:02:23,477 --> 00:02:27,188
OH, IT'S ME AND LAPOOH.

61
00:02:27,230 --> 00:02:29,775
WOW, I MISS THAT DOG.

62
00:02:29,817 --> 00:02:32,903
WELL, YOU CAN ALSO FIND HIM
UNDER "DOG" AND "DEAD."

63
00:02:35,072 --> 00:02:36,156
GREAT, THANKS.

64
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,365
ALL RIGHT.

65
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:38,826
HAND ME THAT OTHER
BOX OF PHOTOS.

66
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:39,994
THAT'S THE VERY LAST ONE.

67
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:41,369
OKAY.

68
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:42,412
( screams )

69
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:47,668
OOPS.

70
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,168
SORRY.

71
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,212
WELL, GOOD THING
YOU NUMBERED ALL OF THEM, HUH?

72
00:02:51,254 --> 00:02:56,051
I HADN'T.
PHOTO 152 WAS A PROTOTYPE.

73
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:58,971
OH, HONEY, HONEY, HONEY,
IT'S OKAY, IT'S OKAY.

74
00:02:59,013 --> 00:03:01,515
HONEY, HOW ABOUT
I FIX YOU A DRINK, HUH?

75
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:02,724
MAYBE A MARGARITA?

76
00:03:02,766 --> 00:03:04,685
ROSS HAS
THE BLENDER.

77
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:07,604
OH, EVERYTHING'S
JUST FALLING APART.

78
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:10,774
NO, HONEY, IT'S OKAY.

79
00:03:10,816 --> 00:03:12,609
LISTEN, I'LL GO TO ROSS'S,
GET THE BLENDER.

80
00:03:12,651 --> 00:03:14,569
YOU GET
ALL THE MARGARITA STUFF READY.

81
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:15,863
HIS KEYS ARE IN THE DRAWER.

82
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:17,614
YOU KNOW WHAT?
ALSO, I NEED SOME CASH.

83
00:03:17,656 --> 00:03:19,366
YOU WANT ME TO STOP
AT THE A.T.M.?

84
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:22,953
NO. WHILE YOU'RE AT ROSS'S,
IF YOU SEE ANY LYING AROUND.

85
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,497
WHAT?

86
00:03:25,539 --> 00:03:28,458
WHAT? I-I-I DON'T,
I DON'T DO THAT.

87
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:42,556
THAT WAS SO COOL, MAN,
THAT WAY YOU LEANED ON THAT GUY.

88
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:45,767
IT IS STARTING
TO GET DARK OUT THERE.

89
00:03:45,809 --> 00:03:46,977
HE TOLD YOU EVERYTHING.

90
00:03:47,019 --> 00:03:48,687
I MEAN,
YOU TOTALLY CRACKED HIM.

91
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:50,605
YEAH, WELL, BEING
THAT HE WAS THE VICTIM.

92
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:52,149
THEY'RE USUALLY
PRETTY TALKATIVE.

93
00:03:52,191 --> 00:03:55,986
OKAY, BUT IT IS OFFICIALLY
NIGHTTIME.

94
00:03:56,028 --> 00:03:59,406
ALL RIGHT, GARY, DO YOU WANT ME
TO GRAB THE BERRY FOR YOU?

95
00:03:59,447 --> 00:04:00,532
IT'S CALLED A CHERRY.

96
00:04:00,574 --> 00:04:03,118
CHANDLER!

97
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:05,871
( laughing )

98
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:08,916
OKAY.

99
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:10,333
I GOT IT.

100
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:13,795
THIS PLACE MAKES
THE BEST SANDWICH IN THE WORLD.

101
00:04:13,837 --> 00:04:15,797
HEY, JOE, DOES IT
HAVE MEATBALLS ON IT?

102
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:16,924
OH, YEAH.

103
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:18,800
MELTED CHEESE AND
MARINARA SAUCE?

104
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:20,260
YUP.

105
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:22,262
YEAH, YOU CAN'T EAT
THAT IN MY CAR.

106
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:26,391
YEAH, OKAY.

107
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:29,811
EVEN THOUGH MY TAX DOLLARS
PAID FOR THIS CAR.

108
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:32,606
YOUR TAX DOLLARS?

109
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:36,985
YEAH, OKAY.

110
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,493
WOW, THAT SANDWICH
REALLY DOES SMELL GOOD.

111
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:47,579
DID I SAY
YOU COULD SMELL IT?

112
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:49,915
I CAN'T SMELL YOUR SANDWICH?

113
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:52,167
HALF THE TASTE
IS IN THE SMELL.

114
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:54,962
YOU'RE SUCKING UP
ALL THE TASTE UNITS.

115
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:56,504
OKAY, I'LL GIVE THEM BACK.

116
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:58,006
( blowing air out nose )

117
00:04:59,549 --> 00:05:02,219
WHAT IS SO GREAT
ABOUT THAT SANDWICH?

118
00:05:02,261 --> 00:05:05,597
OKAY, IMAGINE
THE BEST SEX YOU EVER HAD.

119
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:06,890
OKAY.

120
00:05:06,932 --> 00:05:08,558
ARE YOU THINKING
ABOUT MONICA?

121
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,060
YEAH.

122
00:05:10,102 --> 00:05:11,270
YEAH, WHAT'S THAT LIKE?

123
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:23,907
( yells )

124
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:26,243
OH, PLEASE DON'T BE
FROM A REAL DINOSAUR.

125
00:05:26,285 --> 00:05:27,661
PLEASE, PLEASE.

126
00:05:27,702 --> 00:05:31,248
PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE.
PLEASE, PLEASE, PLEASE.

127
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:34,501
"MADE IN MEXICO." YES!

128
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:37,879
OH. WHO WOULD BUY THIS?

129
00:05:40,174 --> 00:05:41,716
OH.

130
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:44,761
( phone ringing )

131
00:05:44,803 --> 00:05:47,597
Monica:
Rach, it's me. Pick up.

132
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:51,226
HEY, WHAT'S UP?

133
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,436
I need a few more things
to make the margaritas.

134
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:59,067
UM, I NEED SOME, UH, SOME SALT,
SOME MARGARITA MIX, AND TEQUILA.

135
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:01,820
SO ALL WE HAD WAS ICE?

136
00:06:01,862 --> 00:06:03,738
SEE IF HE HAS ICE.

137
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,657
OKAY.

138
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,958
( phone ringing )

139
00:06:16,168 --> 00:06:17,418
( beeping )

140
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:18,670
Hello, Ross?

141
00:06:18,712 --> 00:06:20,297
It's Emily here.

142
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:22,632
I know this is out of the blue,
but, um

143
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:24,467
I'm getting married tomorrow.

144
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,970
Well... maybe I am.

145
00:06:27,012 --> 00:06:28,972
I keep thinking about you

146
00:06:29,014 --> 00:06:31,766
and I'm wondering
if we made a mistake

147
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,143
giving up so fast.

148
00:06:33,185 --> 00:06:35,103
Are you thinking about me?

149
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:37,022
No, of course you're not.

150
00:06:37,064 --> 00:06:38,940
But if you are, call me tonight.

151
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,150
Okay, bye.

152
00:06:40,192 --> 00:06:43,111
OH! OH!

153
00:06:49,450 --> 00:06:50,911
Ross:
SO, WHERE WE GOING NEXT?

154
00:06:50,952 --> 00:06:52,829
THIS WITNESS WON'T
RETURN MY CALLS

155
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:53,788
SO WE'RE GOING TO SEE

156
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,915
IF WE CAN SURPRISE
HIM COMING HOME.

157
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,333
S-SURPRISE HIM?

158
00:06:56,375 --> 00:06:58,793
WE'RE NOT GOING
TO MAKE ANYBODY
MAD, ARE WE?

159
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,337
COME ON, MAN.

160
00:07:00,379 --> 00:07:03,840
SO, YOU GOING TO SQUEEZE
THE PERP'S SHOES A LITTLE BIT

161
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:05,424
BEFORE HE LAWYERS UP?

162
00:07:05,466 --> 00:07:08,136
IT'S A WITNESS, NOT A PERP,
AND NO ONE TALKS LIKE THAT.

163
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:12,224
YEAH, NO ONE TALKS LIKE THAT.

164
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:13,892
OH, WHAT? LIKE YOU'RE MR. COP?

165
00:07:13,934 --> 00:07:15,560
HEY, I'M MORE COP
THAN YOU TWO.

166
00:07:15,602 --> 00:07:16,853
HOW DO YOU FIGURE THAT?

167
00:07:16,895 --> 00:07:18,063
HELLO.

168
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:20,481
I'M IN
THE FRONT SEAT, OKAY.

169
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:23,568
I'M GARY'S PARTNER.

170
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:25,653
YOU KNOW, WHEN
YOU SAY "PARTNER"

171
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:27,155
IT DOESN'T SOUND COP.

172
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:28,823
IT SOUNDS GAY.

173
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:32,744
UM, JEALOUS.

174
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:33,995
HEY, DO YOU MIND?

175
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,622
WE'RE UNDERCOVER HERE.

176
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:37,165
OH, YEAH. NO PROBLEM.

177
00:07:37,207 --> 00:07:38,333
ROSS.

178
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:39,667
SORRY, SORRY.

179
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:42,003
THERE.

180
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:46,841
HEY, GARY, WHO AM I?

181
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:49,677
( imitating E.T. ):
PHONE HOME.

182
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:53,056
LOOK AT OFFICER ROSS

183
00:07:53,098 --> 00:07:55,225
RIDING BACK HERE
WITH THE VISITORS.

184
00:07:55,267 --> 00:07:58,519
YEAH, WHAT'S UP WITH THAT,
SERPICO?

185
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,359
Emily:
Are you thinking about me?

186
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:05,860
No, of course you're not.

187
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,988
But if you are, call me tonight.

188
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:09,823
Okay, bye.

189
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:14,661
NO!

190
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:16,371
I KNOW.

191
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:18,039
WELL, THANK GOD
YOU WERE HERE.

192
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:20,792
I MEAN, WE HAVE
TO ERASE THAT.

193
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,877
WHAT? WE CAN'T DO THAT.

194
00:08:22,919 --> 00:08:24,296
WE HAVE TO.

195
00:08:24,338 --> 00:08:26,173
WHAT IF ROSS HEARS THAT,
AND THEN CALLS HER BACK

196
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:27,590
AND THEN THEY GET
BACK TOGETHER?

197
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:28,716
IS THAT WHAT YOU WANT--

198
00:08:28,758 --> 00:08:30,551
ROSS BACK WITH
THAT CONTROLLING

199
00:08:30,593 --> 00:08:32,720
NEUROTIC, CRAZY EMILY?

200
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,431
EMILY THAT WOULDN'T
LET HIM SEE YOU?

201
00:08:34,473 --> 00:08:37,351
NO! OH, NO. NO. GOD, NO.

202
00:08:37,392 --> 00:08:39,519
HE SHOULD NOT GET BACK TOGETHER
WITH HER.

203
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,355
I MEAN, I KNOW THAT,
YOU KNOW THAT

204
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:43,064
EVEN ROSS KNOWS THAT.

205
00:08:43,106 --> 00:08:45,859
BUT THAT STILL DOESN'T GIVE US
THE RIGHT TO ERASE HIS MESSAGE.

206
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,069
LOOK, I'M HIS SISTER,
OKAY? AND I LOVE HIM.

207
00:08:48,111 --> 00:08:49,946
I DON'T WANT TO
SEE HIM GET HURT.

208
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:53,033
COME ON, DOESN'T THAT GIVE ME
THE RIGHT TO CONTROL HIM...?

209
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:56,911
HELP HIM?

210
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:59,831
I DON'T THINK
HE'S THE ONE WHO NEEDS HELP.

211
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:03,584
LOOK. SHE'S OBVIOUSLY
UNSTABLE, OKAY?

212
00:09:03,626 --> 00:09:06,380
SHE'S THINKING ABOUT
RUNNING OUT ON
HER WEDDING DAY.

213
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:11,926
OKAY, FINE.

214
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:14,595
BUT LOOK AT THE POSITION
SHE'S PUTTING HIM IN.

215
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:16,056
WHAT'S HE'S GOING TO DO?

216
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:19,100
ROSS IS GOING TO RUN OVER
THERE ON THE WEDDING DAY

217
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,685
AND BREAK UP THE MARRIAGE?

218
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,354
I MEAN, WHO WOULD DO THAT?

219
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,900
OKAY, FINE. ALL RIGHT?

220
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:29,610
BUT, THAT'S, YOU KNOW,
THAT WAS DIFFERENT.

221
00:09:29,652 --> 00:09:32,280
ALTHOUGH IT DID INVOLVE
A LOT OF THE SAME PEOPLE.

222
00:09:32,322 --> 00:09:33,323
OH...!

223
00:09:33,365 --> 00:09:34,699
THIS IS OBVIOUSLY

224
00:09:34,741 --> 00:09:37,118
SOME TWISTED JOKE SHE'S
TRYING TO PLAY ON HIM.

225
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,412
OKAY, YOU ARE CRAZY.

226
00:09:38,453 --> 00:09:40,621
I'M SORRY,
BUT SHE SOUNDED GENUINELY UPSET.

227
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:42,040
I MEAN, LISTEN.

228
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:44,209
Male voice:
Your messages have been erased.

229
00:09:44,251 --> 00:09:46,711
NO!

230
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:51,383
OKAY, BUT YOU KNOW,
W-WE'RE SAFE, RIGHT?

231
00:09:51,425 --> 00:09:53,427
I MEAN, NOTHING BAD
IS GOING TO GO DOWN?

232
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:54,553
Gary:
NO.

233
00:09:54,593 --> 00:09:55,929
BUT THAT REMINDS ME.
SIGN THIS.

234
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,097
WHAT IS IT?

235
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,139
IT'S NOTHING.

236
00:09:58,181 --> 00:09:59,433
IT SAYS YOU CAN'T
SUE THE CITY

237
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:00,641
IF YOU SCRAPE YOUR KNEE

238
00:10:00,683 --> 00:10:02,310
OR, YOU KNOW, GET
YOUR HEAD BLOWN OFF.

239
00:10:04,104 --> 00:10:05,730
OH, HURRY UP.

240
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:07,441
I WANT TO SIGN THAT.

241
00:10:07,482 --> 00:10:08,900
OKAY, HERE HE COMES.

242
00:10:08,942 --> 00:10:11,403
Gary:
WHAT IS HE DOING?

243
00:10:11,445 --> 00:10:12,737
WHAT THE HELL IS HE DOING?

244
00:10:12,779 --> 00:10:14,489
WHAT IS IT?
IS EVERYTHING OKAY?

245
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:15,698
WHAT'S GOING ON?

246
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,784
OKAY, HE SEES US.
DON'T MOVE.

247
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:19,619
AND DON'T LOOK
AT HIM.

248
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,871
( loud bang )

249
00:10:33,632 --> 00:10:35,218
HEY, IT'S OKAY.

250
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,678
IT WAS JUST A
CAR BACKFIRE.

251
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,264
HEY, LOOK AT THAT.

252
00:10:39,306 --> 00:10:41,266
YOU TRIED TO SAVE YOUR BUDDY.

253
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:43,642
YOU SEE THAT?

254
00:10:43,684 --> 00:10:45,853
YOU SEE
WHAT HE DID?

255
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:48,315
YOU OKAY, MAN?

256
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:50,942
UH-HUH.

257
00:10:50,984 --> 00:10:52,611
THANKS, JOEY.

258
00:10:54,112 --> 00:10:56,281
UH, HELLO!

259
00:10:58,992 --> 00:11:00,619
HI?

260
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:08,042
I GUESS WE SHOULD GO.

261
00:11:08,084 --> 00:11:09,169
NO. WAIT, WAIT.

262
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:11,212
OH, YEAH, RIGHT.

263
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:12,880
NO. MONICA...

264
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:15,258
MONICA, WE HAVE TO FIX THIS.

265
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:16,468
THERE'S NOTHING WE CAN DO.

266
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:17,676
YOU'VE ERASED THE MESSAGE.

267
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:19,429
YEAH, WELL, UNLESS WE TELL HIM.

268
00:11:19,471 --> 00:11:21,889
LOOK, IF YOU'RE GOING TO BE
TOTALLY RATIONAL ABOUT THIS

269
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:22,932
I CAN'T ARGUE WITH YOU.

270
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:24,725
ALL RIGHT?

271
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,520
FINE. IF YOU WANT TO TELL HIM,
TELL HIM.

272
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:28,355
I JUST,
I DON'T WANT TO BE A PART OF IT.

273
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:29,939
( phone ringing )

274
00:11:29,981 --> 00:11:32,066
OH! MAYBE THAT'S EMILY
CALLING BACK

275
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,444
TO LEAVE THE EXACT SAME MESSAGE.

276
00:11:34,486 --> 00:11:36,237
Ross:
Hey, Ross, it's you.

277
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:39,115
I just want you
to remember this feeling.

278
00:11:39,157 --> 00:11:42,410
You are lucky to be alive

279
00:11:42,452 --> 00:11:46,080
so live every day
to the fullest.

280
00:11:46,122 --> 00:11:49,125
Love yourself, okay? Okay.

281
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:51,586
Oh, and also, get stamps. Bye.

282
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,964
WOW.
PLAY THAT MESSAGE FOR EMILY

283
00:11:55,006 --> 00:11:56,799
AND THIS WHOLE PROBLEM
GOES AWAY.

284
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,301
OH, RIGHT.

285
00:11:59,511 --> 00:12:01,555
HEY, ANYBODY WANT
TO MEET A HERO?

286
00:12:01,596 --> 00:12:03,973
JOHN GLENN IS HERE?

287
00:12:04,015 --> 00:12:05,642
NO, JOEY.

288
00:12:05,684 --> 00:12:07,810
PHEEBS, WE HAD THE
MOST INCREDIBLE NIGHT.

289
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:09,312
OKAY, SO, WE'RE
IN THE CAR...

290
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:10,522
WAIT, HOLD ON.

291
00:12:12,607 --> 00:12:14,484
HI.
HI.

292
00:12:14,526 --> 00:12:17,028
OKAY, GO AHEAD.

293
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:18,154
OKAY, OKAY

294
00:12:18,196 --> 00:12:19,614
SO, WE'RE IN
THE CAR, RIGHT?

295
00:12:19,656 --> 00:12:20,990
AND BANG! A SHOT WAS FIRED

296
00:12:21,032 --> 00:12:24,994
AND JOEY, WITH NO REGARD
FOR HIS OWN SAFETY

297
00:12:25,036 --> 00:12:26,996
THROWS HIMSELF ON ME.

298
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:28,373
OH, MY GOD, JOEY.

299
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:31,792
IT WAS A CAR BACKFIRE.

300
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:33,294
YEAH, BUT HE
DIDN'T KNOW THAT.

301
00:12:33,336 --> 00:12:34,671
YEAH, I DIDN'T KNOW THAT.

302
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:39,676
AND IT COULD HAVE JUST AS EASILY
HAVE BEEN A BULLET.

303
00:12:39,718 --> 00:12:41,720
HEY, JOEY, EVER THINK
ABOUT JOINING THE FORCE?

304
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:42,970
WE COULD USE
A GUY LIKE YOU.

305
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:45,557
WHO JUMPS AT LOUD NOISES.

306
00:12:46,558 --> 00:12:48,351
WOW.

307
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:50,228
I COULD HAVE DIED TONIGHT.

308
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:53,314
YEAH, IF THE CAR THAT BACKFIRED
HAD RUN OVER YOU.

309
00:12:53,356 --> 00:12:54,815
YOU KNOW WHAT?

310
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:57,068
I'M GOING TO GO
HOME BEFORE ROSS
STARTS RAMBLING

311
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,819
ABOUT HIS NEWFOUND
RESPECT FOR LIFE.

312
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:02,741
I DO HAVE
A NEWFOUND RESPECT FOR LIFE.

313
00:13:02,781 --> 00:13:05,410
OH, MY GOD.

314
00:13:08,121 --> 00:13:10,081
SO, YOU WANT
TO GET SOME DINNER?

315
00:13:10,123 --> 00:13:11,249
YEAH, SURE.

316
00:13:11,291 --> 00:13:12,833
YEAH.
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

317
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:16,463
IF I HEARD A SHOT RIGHT NOW,
I'D THROW MY BODY ON YOU.

318
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:17,964
OH, YEAH? WELL,
MAYBE YOU AND I

319
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:20,007
SHOULD TAKE A WALK
IN A BAD NEIGHBORHOOD.

320
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:21,884
OKAY.
ALL RIGHT.

321
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:23,470
BYE.

322
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:24,679
BYE.
BYE.

323
00:13:28,475 --> 00:13:29,559
CUT IT OUT, ROSS.

324
00:13:29,601 --> 00:13:31,436
I'D HATE TO HAVE
TO SAVE YOUR LIFE

325
00:13:31,478 --> 00:13:33,438
AND KICK YOUR ASS
IN THE SAME DAY.

326
00:13:42,489 --> 00:13:43,782
DUDE?

327
00:13:43,822 --> 00:13:46,159
HOW COME YOU TOOK OFF?

328
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:48,662
OH, JUST GOING FOR A WALK.

329
00:13:48,703 --> 00:13:51,790
AROUND THE LIVING ROOM.
WHATEVER.

330
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:53,291
IS SOMETHING WRONG?

331
00:13:53,333 --> 00:13:56,043
NO. NO, I'M JUST TIRED.

332
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,504
YOU KNOW, FROM THE WALK.

333
00:13:59,046 --> 00:14:00,674
OH. OKAY.

334
00:14:00,715 --> 00:14:02,342
YOU DOVE IN FRONT OF ROSS.

335
00:14:03,635 --> 00:14:05,428
ROSS.

336
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:07,972
THAT'S WHAT THIS IS ABOUT.

337
00:14:09,848 --> 00:14:13,186
OH, MY GOD. YOU HATE ROSS.

338
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:15,188
I DON'T HATE ROSS.

339
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:16,230
OF COURSE YOU DO.

340
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,816
I SAVED HIM.
YOU'RE MAD AT ME.

341
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,359
IT ALL ADDS UP.

342
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,487
YOU WANT ROSS OUT
OF THE PICTURE.

343
00:14:22,529 --> 00:14:23,988
WHAT PICTURE?

344
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:25,990
I DON'T KNOW,
BUT I DON'T LIKE
WHAT I'M HEARING.

345
00:14:26,032 --> 00:14:29,202
LOOK, I'M VERY GLAD
THAT YOU SAVED ROSS
FROM THE CAR BACKFIRE

346
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:30,911
BUT IT COULD HAVE BEEN
A BULLET

347
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:33,164
AND, YOU KNOW,
YOU DIDN'T TRY TO SAVE ME.

348
00:14:33,206 --> 00:14:34,999
OH.

349
00:14:35,041 --> 00:14:38,461
YOU'RE UPSET BECAUSE
YOU THINK I CHOSE
ROSS OVER YOU.

350
00:14:38,503 --> 00:14:43,132
NO. I KNEW YOU COULD
TAKE CARE OF YOURSELF.

351
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:44,175
YOU KNOW?

352
00:14:44,217 --> 00:14:45,844
I MEAN, ROSS, HE NEEDS HELP.

353
00:14:45,885 --> 00:14:47,303
HE'S NOT STREET LIKE US.

354
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:48,847
COME ON, WHAT IT COMES DOWN TO

355
00:14:48,887 --> 00:14:50,598
IS YOU WOULD RISK YOUR LIFE
FOR ROSS

356
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:51,850
BEFORE YOU WOULD FOR ME.

357
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,017
THAT'S THE BOTTOM LINE.

358
00:14:53,059 --> 00:14:55,978
N-NO, NOT EXACTLY.

359
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,814
ALL RIGHT, LOOK. I...

360
00:14:57,856 --> 00:15:01,025
I WASN'T TRYING TO SAVE ROSS

361
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:03,110
OKAY?

362
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:05,988
MY SANDWICH WAS NEXT TO ROSS.

363
00:15:08,491 --> 00:15:10,535
ALL RIGHT?

364
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:13,621
I WA... I WAS TRYING
TO SAVE MY SANDWICH.

365
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:17,958
FROM A BULLET?

366
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,545
I KNOW
IT DOESN'T MAKE MUCH SENSE.

367
00:15:20,587 --> 00:15:22,881
MUCH SENSE?

368
00:15:22,921 --> 00:15:24,632
CHANDLER, IT WAS INSTINCT, OKAY?

369
00:15:24,674 --> 00:15:25,884
I JUST WENT FOR IT.

370
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:28,344
SO YOU RISKED YOUR LIFE
FOR A SANDWICH?

371
00:15:28,386 --> 00:15:31,556
I KNOW IT SOUNDS CRAZY,
BUT, CHANDLER

372
00:15:31,598 --> 00:15:35,602
THIS IS THE GREATEST SANDWICH
IN THE WORLD.

373
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:40,231
SO YOU DIDN'T, UH,
CHOOSE ROSS BEFORE ME?

374
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:42,901
NO. I WOULD
NEVER DO THAT.

375
00:15:42,942 --> 00:15:45,027
YOU'RE LIKE MY BROTHER.

376
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:46,696
REALLY?

377
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:48,907
YEAH. IN FACT

378
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:52,159
TO PROVE HOW MUCH
YOU MEAN TO ME...

379
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:58,332
HERE.

380
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,126
THANKS.

381
00:16:00,167 --> 00:16:02,128
OH, EASY, IT'S NOT A HOT DOG.

382
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:10,094
HOW GOOD IS THAT?

383
00:16:10,136 --> 00:16:12,597
( garbled ):
OH, YEAH.

384
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:13,807
SEE?
MM-HMM.

385
00:16:13,848 --> 00:16:15,642
OH, DUDE, WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

386
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:19,604
I THOUGHT YOU WERE SHOWING ME
HOW MUCH I MEAN TO YOU.

387
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:21,606
YEAH. WITH A BITE.

388
00:16:21,648 --> 00:16:23,483
( chuckling ):
GEEZ!

389
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:32,784
( keys jingling )

390
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,668
HEY, HI.

391
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,461
RACH, WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

392
00:16:43,503 --> 00:16:44,963
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

393
00:16:45,003 --> 00:16:47,924
YOU ARE IN OUR APARTMENT
ALL THE TIME, OKAY?

394
00:16:47,966 --> 00:16:50,844
THIS IS JUST A DROP
IN THE BUCKET, MISTER.

395
00:16:50,885 --> 00:16:53,179
YOU KNOW, IT DOESN'T MATTER.

396
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:56,432
THE IMPORTANT THING
IS THAT YOU'RE HERE.

397
00:16:56,474 --> 00:16:59,226
YOU'RE MY FRIEND,
AND YOU'RE HERE.

398
00:17:04,064 --> 00:17:06,442
HUH. OKAY.
JUST A LITTLE SCARED.

399
00:17:06,484 --> 00:17:08,152
WHAT'S GOING ON, ROSS?

400
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:11,322
THE MOST AMAZING THING
HAPPENED TONIGHT.

401
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:13,574
I THOUGHT MY NUMBER WAS UP.

402
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:16,619
I HAD AN ACTUAL
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCE.

403
00:17:16,661 --> 00:17:18,830
WHAT?! WHAT HAPPENED?

404
00:17:18,872 --> 00:17:21,040
WE WERE ON THE RIDE-ALONG
WITH GARY, RIGHT?

405
00:17:21,081 --> 00:17:22,709
AND SOMEBODY TOOK A SHOT AT ME.

406
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,293
( gasping )

407
00:17:25,837 --> 00:17:27,129
REALLY?

408
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,507
NO, A CAR BACKFIRED, BUT...

409
00:17:31,676 --> 00:17:35,596
I THOUGHT SOMEBODY WAS
TAKING A SHOT AT ME

410
00:17:35,638 --> 00:17:37,640
AND, RACH, I, I SURVIVED.

411
00:17:37,682 --> 00:17:39,225
AND I WAS
FILLED WITH

412
00:17:39,266 --> 00:17:42,353
THIS, THIS GREAT
RESPECT FOR LIFE.

413
00:17:42,395 --> 00:17:46,357
YOU KNOW, I WANT TO
EXPERIENCE EVERY MOMENT.

414
00:17:46,399 --> 00:17:49,527
I WANT TO SEIZE
EVERY OPPORTUNITY.

415
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:53,364
I AM SEEING EVERYTHING
SO, SO CLEARLY NOW.

416
00:17:53,406 --> 00:17:56,034
BECAUSE A CAR BACKFIRED?

417
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:58,703
OKAY, WHY ARE YOU HERE?

418
00:17:58,745 --> 00:18:03,541
WELL, I DON'T KNOW HOW THIS FITS
INTO YOUR WHOLE SEIZING THING

419
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:06,168
BUT, UM, EMILY CALLED YOU TODAY.

420
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,421
YOU TALKED TO HER?

421
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:10,089
NO, SHE LEFT
A MESSAGE.

422
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,008
BUT IT KIND OF GOT ERASED.

423
00:18:12,050 --> 00:18:13,384
I MEAN, THERE'S...

424
00:18:13,426 --> 00:18:15,595
SOMETHING WRONG
WITH YOUR MACHINE.

425
00:18:15,636 --> 00:18:17,680
OKAY, WHAT DID SHE SAY?

426
00:18:17,722 --> 00:18:19,057
WELL, UM, SOMETHING

427
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,768
ABOUT HAVING SECOND THOUGHTS
ABOUT THE WEDDING

428
00:18:21,809 --> 00:18:25,063
AND DID YOU GUYS MAKE A MISTAKE
BREAKING UP, AND, UH

429
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,981
SHE WANTS YOU TO CALL HER.

430
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,776
WOW.

431
00:18:29,817 --> 00:18:33,029
NOW THAT WAS A GOOD THING
THAT I TOLD YOU, RIGHT?

432
00:18:33,071 --> 00:18:34,948
HUH? YEAH. YES.

433
00:18:34,989 --> 00:18:36,323
OF COURSE.

434
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:37,324
OKAY, THANK YOU.

435
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:38,868
THANK YOU, BECAUSE

436
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:41,621
I'M GOING TO JUST GO TELL MONICA
THAT I WAS RIGHT.

437
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:42,789
BECAUSE YOU KNOW WHAT?

438
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,331
SHE DIDN'T WANT...
NOT IMPORTANT.

439
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:46,166
THE POINT IS, I WAS RIGHT.

440
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,460
YOUR DECISION.

441
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:51,047
OKAY? I WAS RIGHT.

442
00:18:51,089 --> 00:18:52,966
YOUR DECISION.

443
00:18:53,007 --> 00:18:54,717
RIGHT.

444
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:57,095
I GUESS I SHOULD CALL EMILY.

445
00:18:57,136 --> 00:19:00,056
OKAY. NO,
THAT'S NOT THE RIGHT DECISION.

446
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:01,348
THAT'S NOT RIGHT.

447
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,767
ROSS, COME ON.

448
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:06,896
I MEAN, THAT WOMAN
MADE YOU MISERABLE.

449
00:19:06,938 --> 00:19:08,648
OKAY, ROSS

450
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:11,400
DO YOU REALLY WANT TO
GET BACK INTO THAT?

451
00:19:11,442 --> 00:19:13,069
OKAY, LOOK, YESTERDAY

452
00:19:13,111 --> 00:19:16,948
I WOULDN'T HAVE EVEN CONSIDERED
CALLING HER BACK

453
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:19,575
BUT MY EX-WIFE CALLS

454
00:19:19,617 --> 00:19:23,287
ON THE SAME DAY
I HAVE A NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCE?

455
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,790
I MEAN, THAT'S GOT
TO MEAN SOMETHING, RIGHT?

456
00:19:25,832 --> 00:19:28,835
ROSS, THAT WAS NOT A
NEAR-DEATH EXPERIENCE.

457
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:30,962
THAT WAS BARELY
AN EXPERIENCE.

458
00:19:31,004 --> 00:19:33,297
YOU WEREN'T THERE.

459
00:19:34,841 --> 00:19:38,803
OKAY, MAYBE THIS IS SOMETHING
I'M SUPPOSED TO SEIZE, YOU KNOW?

460
00:19:38,845 --> 00:19:41,221
OKAY. YOU KNOW WHAT?

461
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:45,726
MAYBE THIS IS NOT
ABOUT SEIZING STUFF.

462
00:19:45,768 --> 00:19:49,856
MAYBE THIS IS ABOUT
ESCAPING STUFF.

463
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:51,983
OKAY, I MEAN,
LOOK AT TODAY.

464
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:53,776
I MEAN, YOU ESCAPED...

465
00:19:53,818 --> 00:19:55,402
DEATH...

466
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:57,404
YOU KNOW?

467
00:19:57,446 --> 00:20:00,616
AND MAYBE THIS
IS A CHANCE FOR
YOU TO ESCAPE

468
00:20:00,658 --> 00:20:02,994
GETTING BACK TOGETHER
WITH EMILY.

469
00:20:03,036 --> 00:20:05,997
THAT DOES MAKE SENSE.

470
00:20:06,039 --> 00:20:08,166
BECAUSE I DO

471
00:20:08,206 --> 00:20:10,960
WANT TO SEIZE SOME OPPORTUNITY

472
00:20:11,002 --> 00:20:15,381
BUT I REALLY DON'T WANT
TO SEE OR TALK TO HER.

473
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:18,843
THEN, THERE YOU GO.

474
00:20:18,885 --> 00:20:20,178
YEAH.

475
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:22,429
YEAH, MAYBE TODAY'S JUST...

476
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:25,183
CLOSE CALL DAY.

477
00:20:27,393 --> 00:20:29,353
HEY, THANKS, RACH.

478
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:31,271
OH, HONEY, NO PROBLEM.

479
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:32,690
OKAY.
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

480
00:20:32,732 --> 00:20:34,192
THE MESSAGE IS BLINKING.

481
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,818
MAYBE YOU DIDN'T ERASE IT.

482
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:37,028
OH?

483
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,487
Hey, Ross, it's you.

484
00:20:38,529 --> 00:20:39,822
OH, YEAH.

485
00:20:39,864 --> 00:20:41,532
THAT'S AN OLD MESSAGE.

486
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:43,576
NOBODY NEEDS TO HEAR THAT.

487
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:48,039
HEY, UM, WAS MONICA HERE?

488
00:20:48,081 --> 00:20:49,040
YEAH.

489
00:20:49,082 --> 00:20:52,001
YEAH, I WANT MY MONEY BACK.

490
00:20:52,043 --> 00:20:55,088
YEAH, UM, YOU PROBABLY NEED THAT
FOR STAMPS, RIGHT?

491
00:21:04,097 --> 00:21:06,015
HAS GARY EVER BEEN SHOT AT
FOR REAL?

492
00:21:06,057 --> 00:21:07,349
YES, ONCE.

493
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:08,350
YEAH.

494
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:09,685
A LITTLE.

495
00:21:09,727 --> 00:21:12,521
HE KIND OF DID IT TO HIMSELF.

496
00:21:12,563 --> 00:21:15,357
IT'S NOT REALLY A GOOD STORY.

497
00:21:15,399 --> 00:21:18,694
I WONDER HOW I'D REACT
UNDER FIRE, YOU KNOW?

498
00:21:18,736 --> 00:21:21,197
AND NOT BACKFIRE,
BUT HEAVY FIRE.

499
00:21:21,239 --> 00:21:23,157
LIKE IF I WAS IN A WAR
OR SOMETHING.

500
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:25,118
MAN, I WOULD BE
GREAT IN A WAR.

501
00:21:25,159 --> 00:21:28,788
I MEAN, I THINK I WOULD MAKE
A FANTASTIC MILITARY LEADER.

502
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:31,040
I MEAN, I KNOW I
WOULD MAKE GENERAL

503
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:32,541
BEFORE ANY OF YOU GUYS.

504
00:21:32,583 --> 00:21:36,378
BEFORE OR AFTER YOU WERE SHOT
BY YOUR OWN TROOPS?

505
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,671
I KNOW WHERE JOEY WOULD BE.

506
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:38,714
HE'D BE IN THE FOXHOLE

507
00:21:38,756 --> 00:21:40,424
PROTECTING
ALL OF US.

508
00:21:40,466 --> 00:21:43,594
YES, IF THE FOXHOLE
WAS LINED WITH SANDWICHES.

509
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:47,014
YEAH, HERO SANDWICHES.

510
00:21:49,142 --> 00:21:50,977
WELL, YOU ALL KNOW
THAT I'M A PACIFIST

511
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:52,979
SO I'M NOT INTERESTED IN WAR
IN ANY WAY

512
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:54,688
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

513
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:57,399
WHEN THE REVOLUTION COMES,
I WILL HAVE TO DESTROY YOU ALL.

514
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:59,610
NOT YOU, JOEY.

515
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:03,656
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

